# What `VIAME_ENABLE_COLMAP` adds.
#
# Its own file because it is 166 MB and only `reconstruction.py` and
# `reconstruct_3d` need it -- `lite-install-size.md` section 3 row 9.
#
# `pycolmap-cuda12` rather than `pycolmap` on a CUDA build: it links the
# system CUDA 12 runtime VIAME already builds against, where the plain wheel
# pulls packaged `cuda-toolkit[cudart,curand]` wheels of its own.
# Compiled with the accelerator's lock as a constraint, so every version
# this shares with a default install is the same version. It deliberately
# does not `-r base.in`: this file is what the option *adds*, and the build
# installs it alongside the accelerator lock rather than instead of it.

pycolmap-cuda12 ; platform_system == "Linux"
pycolmap ; platform_system != "Linux"
